# Grow Project Rules for AI Assistants

## Core Architectural Rules
1. Local-First & Zero Server Cost: All user garden state lives in IndexedDB via Dexie (`src/lib/db.ts`). Never introduce paid databases or persistent WebSocket backend servers that break Vercel's Free Hobby Tier.
2. Never Destructively Wipe Data: When importing or syncing plant data, always use `mergeSeedPackIntoDb` (`src/lib/seed-pack.ts`) so existing user gardens are preserved.
3. Browser Support Policy: Allow web platform features (e.g. Chrome Built-in AI Prompt API, WebMCP) only with strict feature detection (`'LanguageModel' in self`) and graceful fallback.
4. No Version Numbers or License Boilerplate in UI: Never hardcode or display arbitrary semantic version numbers (such as `Grow 1.1.0`) or licensing notices (such as `Open Source under MIT`) in extensions, widgets, or UI components. Version tracking is handled dynamically via Git commits (`src/lib/git-version.ts`) if needed, and licensing is governed repository-wide.
5. Usage Statistics Gathering Standard: Extensions or tools built for usage statistics have the explicit primary purpose of gathering, aggregating, and visualizing usage statistics (sessions, active days, feature invocation frequencies, lifecycle transitions, storage footprint, and AI inference volume) while keeping all telemetry local-first and zero-cost.
6. Zero Git Merge Conflicts: Do NOT edit `src/app/page.tsx` when adding new gardening calculators, widgets, or datasets. Use `src/extensions/<kebab-id>/index.tsx` registered in `src/extensions/registry.ts`.
